Windows: put the Python toolchain's dist/ directory on PATH for the
wheel_installer action.

pycross_wheel_library invokes the wheel_installer py_binary via
ctx.actions.run() with an explicit `env` dict that fully replaces the
default action env. On Windows, the rules_python 2.x launcher.exe
LoadLibrary's python313.dll at process start — if the DLL isn't on
the launcher's DLL search path (which for a Bazel action means the
action-env PATH), it fails with STATUS_DLL_NOT_FOUND (0xC0000135)
before main() runs. python313.dll is co-located with python.exe in
mongo's python-build-standalone toolchain (dist/python.exe +
dist/python313.dll), so adding the toolchain's interpreter dirname to
PATH resolves it. No-op on Linux/macOS.

Applied via `single_version_override(patches=[...])` on rules_pycross
in //MODULE.bazel. Candidate for upstreaming to jvolkman/rules_pycross.

--- a/pycross/private/wheel_library.bzl	2026-07-14 14:22:38
+++ b/pycross/private/wheel_library.bzl	2026-07-14 14:23:57
@@ -31,16 +31,29 @@
     for install_exclude_glob in ctx.attr.install_exclude_globs:
         args.add("--install-exclude-glob", install_exclude_glob)
 
+    # Set environment variables to make generated .pyc files reproducible.
+    env = {
+        "SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH": "315532800",
+        "PYTHONHASHSEED": "0",
+    }
+
+    # On Windows, the rules_python 2.x py_binary launcher LoadLibrary's
+    # python313.dll at process start. Put the toolchain's interpreter
+    # directory (where python313.dll lives, co-located with python.exe
+    # in the python-build-standalone layout) on PATH so the loader
+    # finds it. No-op on Linux/macOS.
+    _py = ctx.toolchains["@rules_python//python:toolchain_type"]
+    if _py and _py.py3_runtime and _py.py3_runtime.interpreter:
+        _interp = _py.py3_runtime.interpreter
+        if _interp.basename.endswith(".exe"):
+            env["PATH"] = _interp.dirname
+
     ctx.actions.run(
         inputs = inputs,
         outputs = [out],
         executable = ctx.executable._tool,
         arguments = [args],
-        # Set environment variables to make generated .pyc files reproducible.
-        env = {
-            "SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH": "315532800",
-            "PYTHONHASHSEED": "0",
-        },
+        env = env,
         mnemonic = "WheelInstall",
         progress_message = "Installing %s" % ctx.file.wheel.basename,
     )
@@ -130,4 +143,5 @@
             executable = True,
         ),
     },
+    toolchains = ["@rules_python//python:toolchain_type"],
 )
